Requirements: 6   with obligations: 6

[task-01] Wherever the `acceptance` tool is installed, when the command starts it loads
    the `.env` file in the working directory, if there is one, before any model call.
    Today the tool has no `.env` loading of its own, so installed as a standalone tool
    and run in another project it sees no API keys at all. A variable already set in the
    environment keeps its value over the one in `.env`. No `.env` file is not an error.
    -> load-working-directory-env-before-model-call  [functional/explicit]
       When the command starts, it loads the `.env` file in the working directory, if
       one exists, before any model call.
    -> env-vars-take-precedence  [invariant/explicit]
       A variable already set in the environment keeps its value over the one in `.env`.
    -> no-dotenv-file-not-an-error  [error_handling/explicit]
       The command starts successfully when no `.env` file is present in the working
       directory.

[task-02] In record mode, the command warns at startup about each key that a model it is
    configured to use would need and that is not set, naming the variable and the model.
    Before the first live call to a model, if that model's key is still missing, the run
    stops with an error that names the variable and the model, and the call is not sent,
    so the user never sees the provider's "invalid API key" reply instead. A run that
    needs no live call, because every request is already recorded or because it runs in
    replay mode, still succeeds without any keys.
    -> startup-warns-missing-model-keys  [functional/explicit]
       At startup, the command warns about each missing key required by any configured
       model, naming both the variable and the model.
    -> missing-key-preflight-error  [functional/explicit]
       Before the first live call to a model, if that model's key is still missing, the
       run stops with an error that names the variable and the model.
    -> call-not-sent  [functional/explicit]
       The live model call is not sent when the required key is still missing before the
       first live call.
    -> hide-provider-invalid-api-key-reply  [error_handling/explicit]
       The user never sees the provider's "invalid API key" reply instead.
    -> no-live-call-succeeds-without-keys  [functional/explicit]
       A run that needs no live call, because every request is already recorded or
       because it runs in replay mode, still succeeds without any keys.

[constraint-01] No model request changes, so every recorded transcript keeps replaying.
    -> preserve-recorded-transcripts-replay  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve the ability for every recorded transcript to keep replaying without any
       model request changes.

[exclusion-01] Reading `.env` from any directory other than the working directory.
    -> no-other-env-directories  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not read `.env` from any directory other than the working
       directory.

[exclusion-02] Warning about, or stopping for, a missing key that the coding agent which
    builds mutation edits needs.
    -> do-not-read-coding-agent-keys  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not read keys for the coding agent which builds mutation edits.

[exclusion-03] A command-line option to name a different `.env` file.
    -> no-cli-option-for-env-file  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not add a command-line option to name a different `.env` file.

